    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-31T09:20:47+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T09:20:47+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T22:50:47Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T22:50:47Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system south of the Bight extends a trough over far southeast of state and will continue to move east clearing the state this morning, followed by a new high pressure system. Another low pressure system is expected to enter from the west on Sunday, moving over central and eastern districts on Monday, followed by another ridge of high pressure which will persist until Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending west to southwesterly in the middle of the day then tending south to southwesterly in the early afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures 30 to 37.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers south of Yunta from the late morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Yunta at night. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h in the early morning then tending northwest to northeasterly in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 41.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northwest to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the day then tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to 20 to 27 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 42.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-04T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-03T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the morning. Sunny afternoon. Winds southeast to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
